Touchscreen swipes as trackpad gestures (Touch.cpp): the touch path synthesizes swipe
begin/update/end into g_pTrackpadGestures, so the configured hl.gesture entries run
live for touch as on the touchpad. Four fingers whose centroid travels
gestures:touch_swipe_threshold px become a 4-finger swipe; a 3-finger tap followed by
three fingers down again (gestures:touch_move_tap_ms, touch_move_gap_ms,
touch_move_slop) becomes a 3-finger swipe -- the `move` gesture, dock card swipe
included. The delta is the centroid's logical-px travel times
gestures:touch_swipe_scale, in finger direction like libinput's; the gesture's
touches are cancelled for the client, a lift ends it, another finger cancels it.
While one runs, g_pTrackpadGestures->m_fromTouchscreen (declared by 04) is set, since
these deltas are logical: the dock card swipe maps them to the physical frame.

